 35CL    34S(3HE,D)                    2017GI09,1969GR23         ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+34}S g.s.                                                 
 35CL c  2017Gi09: a 20-MeV {+3}He{+2+} beam was produced from the MP Van de    
 35CL2c  Graaff tandem accelerator at the Maier-Leibnitz Laboratorium (MLL) and 
 35CL3c  impinged on a 50-|mg/cm{+2} Ag{-2}S 99.999% enriched in {+34}S with a  
 35CL4c  8-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Reaction products were momentum-separated 
 35CL5c  by the Q3D magnetic spectrograph and focused on focal plane detectors  
 35CL6c  consisting of two multiwire proportional counters (MWPCs) and a plastic
 35CL7c  scintillator. Deduced 22 levels, L-transfers, J, |p, spectroscopic     
 35CL8c  factors spectroscopic factors from FRESCO-DWBA analysis, and resonance 
 35CL9c  strengths. Deduced the thermonuclear {+34}S(p,|g){+35}Cl reaction rate 
 35CLAc  through Monte Carlo methods using the STARLIB code. Calculated the     
 35CLBc  {+34}S/{+32}S isotopic ratio using the hydrodynamical nova model SHIVA.
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969Gr23: a 11.0-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the MIT-ONR Van de  
 35CL2c  Graaff generator. The target was 9.3-|mg/cm{+2} {+34}S made by         
 35CL3c  evaporating PbS (67.6%{+34}S) onto a formvar backing. Deuterons were   
 35CL4c  detected on 50 |mm nuclear emulsions in the MIT multiple-gap           
 35CL5c  spectrograph at 23 different angles from 7.5|' to 172.5|'. Measured    
 35CL6c  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced 17 levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic     
 35CL7c  factors from zero-range JULIE-DWBA analysis.                           
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1970Mo01: a 13-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the Argonne tandem Van
 35CL2c  de Graaf accelerator. The target was 200-|mg/cm{+2} 86% enriched       
 35CL3c  {+34}S. Reaction products were detected using two telescopes of silicon
 35CL4c  surface-barrier detectors with FWHM|?80 keV and analyzed by a magnetic 
 35CL5c  spectrograph with FHWM|?20 keV at |q<20|'. Measured |s(E{-d},|q),      
 35CL6c  |q{-c.m.}|?5|' to 100|'. Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers,           
 35CL7c  spectroscopic factors from local, zero-range JULIE-DWBA analysis.      
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1994Ve04: a 25-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the Orsay MP Tandem   
 35CL2c  Van de Graaff accelerator. The target was KCl with natural chlorine.   
 35CL3c  Reaction products were momentum-analyzed by an Enge split-pole magnetic
 35CL4c  spectrograph and detected using a 50-cm long telescope of a            
 35CL5c  position-sensitive proportional counter, proportional |DE counter, and 
 35CL6c  a plastic scintillator. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced J, |p,          
 35CL7c  L-transfer, and spectroscopic factor for the ground state of {+35}Cl   
 35CL8c  from local, zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                            
 35CL cL E$From 1969Gr23 for E(level)<6 MeV and from 2017Gi09 for E(level)>6    
 35CL2cL MeV, unless otherwise noted.                                           
 35CL cL L$From DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q) in 1969Gr23 for E(level)<6 
 35CL2cL MeV and in 2017Gi09 for E(level)>6 MeV, unless otherwise noted.        
 35CL cL $For levels below 6 MeV, spectroscopic factor                          
 35CL2cL (2J+1)C{+2}S=|s(|q){-exp}/|s(|q){-DWBA}/N, where N is a normalization 
 35CL3cL factor. J is the spin of the populated {+35}Cl level. N=4.42 is used in
 35CL4cL 1969Gr23 and 1970Mo01 from 1966Ba54. N=4.43 is used in 1994Ve04. For   
 35CL5cL levels above 6 MeV, C{+2}S values are from 2017Gi09 without using the  
 35CL6cL factor N. 2017Gi09 also states that it is not possible to distinguish  
 35CL7cL between J=L+s or J=L-s coupling given the experimental uncertainties.  
